===============================================================================
RUNNING PHOLD
===============================================================================
===============================================================================
To run PHOLD with default settings on N PEs (Charm++ on Reconverse, which has
no charmrun):
> make
> ./phold +pe N

Across P processes on a Mac, use LCI's lcrun; on a cluster, use srun:
> lcrun -n P ./phold +pe N

To get a list of available options for phold run:
> ./phold --help

===============================================================================
TESTING PHOLD
===============================================================================
===============================================================================
Tests are in test_configs/. Each is a configuration file that sets
expected-events, the number of committed events the run must produce: PHOLD
with x LPs, y initial events per LP and end time z commits the same number of
events regardless of the synchronization protocol, PE count or mapping, and
the simulator aborts if the count does not match.

To run every model configuration under every synchronization configuration at
several PE and process counts, use tests/test.py from the repository root:
> python3 tests/test.py --quick

To add a test case, add a configuration file to test_configs/ with an
expected-events line.
